    {
      "id": "claim_9698b6ee1da447d6ac87a5cfd0e92edc",
      "statement": "slugify() is idempotent on its own output: strings that are already slugs, such as \"hello-world\" or \"already-a-slug\", pass through the pipeline unchanged because they match no transliteration keys, are unaffected by NFKD and lowercasing, have each hyphen mapped to itself by the [^a-z0-9]+ substitution, and carry no boundary hyphens to strip. Re-slugging stored slugs is therefore lossless (test_already_slugified).",
